    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d634">

                <pb facs="0821" n="811" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg811"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.248/3–2847</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Secretary of
                        War</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Patterson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-03-28">March 28, 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Before Secretary
                    Marshall left for Moscow he indicated that he attached great importance to the
                    rapid completion of the civilian end-use portion of the 8⅓ Group Chinese Air
                    Force Program. I would like to make clear that the statement in my letter of
                    March 6, 1947,<anchor n="58" xml:id="d634-f1"/> that first priority for
                    transferable military equipment should be assigned to Greece, was not intended
                    to mean that any action should be taken which would delay the completion of this
                    Chinese program.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dean Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
